Reason: crumbling sand in rm_a3h04 asks tile_exists about the edge tiles it has just deleted, and every miss walked the
room's whole tile array (~4,800 tiles, up to ~4 ms a call on the Wii) to confirm the index (patch 0063 keeps it current
through tile_add and tile_delete; the layer deletes mark it stale). A miss in a current index without repeated ids is
now the answer. The walk was also what healed one case the index can't see: leaving a non-persistent room frees its
tiles, and re-entering reads them again, possibly at the same address and count, so entering a room now marks the
index stale (one rebuild at the room's first tile lookup).
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

--- a/src/vm_builtins.c
+++ b/src/vm_builtins.c
@@ -14718,8 +14718,11 @@
